    "title": "EU and China reach a trade truce in Beijing, but Europe's rare earth exposure remains - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Decode39 ,\n1 days ago The EU and China reached a 16-point agreement to ease trade tensions, including a “green channel” for EU exports of rare earth minerals and magnets. While this provides predictability for European industry, it doesn’t address the EU’s dependence on China for these critical materials. The EU must use this time to develop its own magnet production capacity, especially for defense purposes, to reduce its vulnerability. Read full article",
